 -- wl04 <wl04@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 21:05:21 +0100

gpu-switcher (0.1.0-25) unstable; urgency=low

  * Security: the caller's locale is mapped to the en/ru allowlist before catalog loading, so a caller-controlled locale can no longer hang the root helper.
  * Security: the helper's diagnostic log is bounded (2000-char lines, flattened), rotated (1 MiB, one slot), and rate-limited (20 calls/60 s per sender and method).
  * 3D-controller-class GPUs (PCI 0x030200) are now detected as valid display primaries, in the UI and in the helper.
  * Reset now refreshes udev when the managed rule is already absent, so a previously failed refresh can be retried.
  * When the configured GPU is not currently detected, the app shows a distinct "Configured GPU (not currently detected)" state instead of "auto"; Apply on that state is a guarded no-op pointing at "Reset to auto".
  * The polkit policy is fixed (a single <defaults> block, as the DTD requires) and is validated during every build.
  * Udev verification now distinguishes verified / unsupported / failed: an error, timeout, or missing udevadm is no longer reported as success and never enables the fast-path logout.

 -- wl04 <wl04@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 20:36:23 +0100

gpu-switcher (0.1.0-24) unstable; urgency=low

  * "Log out" now ends the session via the GNOME SessionManager.
  * GNOME detection uses XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP.
  * The "selected primary" journal lookup is scoped to the current session.
  * Operation outcome (success, no change, timed out) is tracked explicitly.
  * D-Bus client timeout is 280 s and bus acquisition is guarded.
  * GPU detection runs in a worker thread while the UI shows "Detecting…".
  * Polkit authorization is bound to the caller's bus name.
  * The DRM udev trigger is settled before the mutter tag is checked.
  * Success now requires the mutter tag in the card's current udev tags.
  * Write failures (verify, backup, rename, unlink) are reported distinctly.
  * GTK 4.10 / gir1.2-gtk-4.0 is now a required dependency.
  * Both .deb build paths converge (same files, man page, msgfmt catalogs).
  * The .deb version is read from the top changelog entry.
  * release.sh generates the orig tarball and cross-checks both builds.
  * Source format is 3.0 (quilt).

